{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_structural_typing", "label": "Structural typing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A is assignable to B when A has at least B's members of compatible types. Names never matter. Extra members are fine; missing ones are not. Opposite of Java nominal typing."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_function_variance", "label": "Function parameter contravariance", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A function may accept less and return more. Returns compare covariantly. Method parameters are bivariant; strictFunctionTypes tightens function-typed properties, not method shorthand."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_branded_types", "label": "Branded types", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "type UserId = string is the same type as OrderId. Brand with string & { readonly __brand: 'UserId' } so the shapes differ. The brand is erased at runtime."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_private_nominal", "label": "Private members are nominal", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two classes with identically named private fields are not interchangeable. Each private declaration is unique to its class \u2014 the one place TypeScript is nominal without a brand."}, {"id": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_read_errors_bottom_up", "label": "Read assignability errors bottom-up", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The innermost Type A is not assignable to type B names the real mismatch. Outer lines are the property path the compiler walked."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_structural_typing", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_04_object_types_excess_property_checks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_structural_typing", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_function_variance", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_structural_typing", "target": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_branded_types", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/typescript/pages/phase-1-type-vocabulary/09-structural-typing.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_typescript_pages_phase_1_type_vocabulary_09_structural_typing_structural_typing", "target": "docs_typesc